<article class="env-lemma" id="099K">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/099K">Lemma <span data-tag="099K">52.6.18</span>.</a> Let $f : (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D}), \mathcal{O}') \to (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}), \mathcal{O})$ be a morphism of ringed topoi. Let $\mathcal{I} \subset \mathcal{O}$ and $\mathcal{I}' \subset \mathcal{O}'$ be finite type sheaves of ideals such that $f^\sharp $ sends $f^{-1}\mathcal{I}$ into $\mathcal{I}'$. Then $Rf_*$ sends $D_{comp}(\mathcal{O}', \mathcal{I}')$ into $D_{comp}(\mathcal{O}, \mathcal{I})$ and has a left adjoint $Lf_{comp}^*$ which is $Lf^*$ followed by derived completion. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The first statement we have seen in Lemma <a href="/tag/099J" data-tag="099J">52.6.7</a>. Note that the second statement makes sense as we have a derived completion functor $D(\mathcal{O}') \to D_{comp}(\mathcal{O}', \mathcal{I}')$ by Proposition <a href="/tag/099F" data-tag="099F">52.6.12</a>. OK, so now let $K \in D_{comp}(\mathcal{O}, \mathcal{I})$ and $M \in D_{comp}(\mathcal{O}', \mathcal{I}')$. Then we have 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (K, Rf_*M) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (Lf^*K, M) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (Lf_{comp}^*K, M)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       by the universal property of derived completion. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>